2. UPSTREAM ATTRIBUTION

   OBD-II sample (the .csv and .parquet files at the repository root):
   DTC code definitions are compiled from a public, MIT-licensed
   compilation of SAE J2012-derived trouble codes. The upstream MIT license
   and copyright notice are preserved in LICENSE-upstream.txt, as required.

   Heavy Duty (J1939) sample (samples/heavyduty/): SPN/FMI fault pairs, OEM
   fault codes and controller assignments are facts taken from fault-code
   documents the manufacturers publish. Each row's source_url and
   source_doc identify its document, and SOURCES.md lists every source.
   Descriptions, explanations, fault families and fixes are written in
   DataEngineered's own words (a parameter name may match the
   manufacturer's own plain name); no sentences from OEM documents, and
   nothing from the SAE J1939 Digital Annex or J1939 DBC files, are
   included. The Heavy Duty sample is licensed under ODbL v1.0 like the
   rest of this repository (Section 1).

